  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing and Sustaining Peace and Security Mechanims through Support to Joint Peace and Security Teams in Mindanao, Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to contribute to addressing newly emerged challenges to achieving GPH-MILF Normalization Process and sustainable peace. IOM will seek to build peaceful communities in BARMM through direct capacity support to the JPSC/JPST during the critical last phases of BARMM&apos;s transition period. Given the sensitivity of the project in engaging with security sectors and MILF combatants, IOM will ensure that Human Rights Due Diligence (HRDD) assessment is undertaken, and risk mitigation plan is crafted to ensure that resources given through the project is used for the specific intended purposes and further ensure that implementation is grounded by principles of &#x2018;Do-No-Harm&#x2019; and &#x2018;conflict-sensitivity&#x2019;. Accessible and functioning complaint and feedback mechanisms, in consultation with JPSC, JPST and communities, will also be established across the project sites from the early stage of the implementation to strengthen accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
